## Run locally

```bash
{{if eq .Database.Engine "postgresql"}}export DATABASE_URL='jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/{{.ProjectName}}'
export DATABASE_USER='postgres'
export DATABASE_PASSWORD='replace-me'
{{else}}export DATABASE_URL='jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/{{.ProjectName}}?useSSL=true&requireSSL=true'
export DATABASE_USER='root'
export DATABASE_PASSWORD='replace-me'
{{end}}mvn spring-boot:run
```

Set `BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL` and `BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD` together on the first
run. The password must contain at least 12 characters. Remove both bootstrap
variables after the account exists. `COOKIE_SECURE` defaults to `true`; set it to
`false` only for local HTTP development.

The service exposes `GET /healthz` for process liveness and `GET /readyz` for a
bounded database readiness check. Browser sessions use an HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax
cookie, while automation uses `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Raw session and API
tokens are returned only to their owners and only SHA-256 digests are persisted.
Database errors are never returned to clients. The HTTP contract is
`api/openapi.yaml`.
{{if .Admin}}

## Administration UI

```bash
cd web/admin
npm ci
npm run dev
```

The Vite development server proxies `/api` and `/healthz` to `localhost:8080`.
Run `npm run lint`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, and `npm run format:check`
before committing changes.
{{end}}

## Verify

```bash
mvn verify
```

The verify lifecycle runs JUnit, ArchUnit, Checkstyle, Spotless, SpotBugs, and the
Maven Enforcer rules. Generated code uses constructor injection and package
boundaries; do not add field injection or a generic utility package.
